+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-add-cancellation/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+## Context
+
+Bookings are kept in an in-memory array in `createRentalService`, each with its parsed `from`/`to`. Overlap checks in `book` and `availability` scan that array. The spec already fixes the policy: under 24 hours before start, no refund; otherwise full refund.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- `at` is parsed as an ISO-8601 UTC instant (any time of day, not only midnight/hour), with the same parser as periods. Invalid `at` throws.
+- Refund is `total` when `start - at >= 24h`, else 0. Exactly 24 hours before start is a full refund, since the policy says "less than 24 hours" gets nothing. `at` after the start gets 0. This is an assumption on the boundary and on late cancellations.
+- Remove the booking from the active list on cancellation, so `book` and `availability` stop seeing it with no further change. Keep the cancelled ids in a set, so a second cancel throws "already cancelled" and not "unknown".
+- Unknown booking id throws.
+- Validate everything (id, `at`) before mutating, so a failed cancel leaves no trace.
+
+## Risks
+
+- A cancellation `at` after the booking ended is accepted and refunds nothing; the request does not say to reject it.
