@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+## Why
+
+Customers ask the desk to cancel bookings. The service can book but not cancel, so the desk has no way to free the equipment or tell the customer what they get back.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+- Apply the cancellation policy already reserved in the spec: no refund when `at` is less than 24 hours before the booking's start, otherwise the full booking total.
+- A cancelled booking stops holding its equipment: it no longer blocks `book` or `availability`.
+- A booking can be cancelled only once; unknown ids and repeat cancellations are errors.
+- **BREAKING (spec only)**: replaces the "Cancellation policy reserved" requirement, which said no cancellation operation is exposed.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `equipment-rental`: adds cancellation, replacing the reserved-policy requirement, and a cancelled booking no longer counts toward overlap or availability.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `RentalService` interface and `createRentalService`.
+- `src/index.test.ts`: new tests.
+- Out of scope: partial refunds, cancellation fees, persistence.
